#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:1
msgid "OneDrive and SharePoint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:3
msgid ""
"Since v0.27.4, xlwings works with locally synced files on OneDrive, OneDrive "
"for Business, and SharePoint. Some constellations will work out-of-the-box, "
"while others require you to edit the configuration via the `xlwings.conf` "
"file (see [User Config](addin.md#user-config-ribbonconfig-file)) or the "
"workbook's `xlwings.conf` sheet (see [Workbook Config](addin.md#workbook-"
"config-xlwingsconf-sheet))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:6
msgid ""
"This documentation is for OneDrive and SharePoint files that are synced to a "
"local folder. This means that both, the Excel and Python file, need to show "
"the green check mark in the File Explorer/Finder as status---a cloud icon "
"will not work. If, in turn, you are looking for the documentation to run "
"xlwings with Excel on the web, see [xlwings Server](https://server.xlwings."
"org)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:9
msgid "An easy workaround if you run into issues is to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:11
msgid ""
"Disable the `ADD_WORKBOOK_TO_PYTHONPATH` setting (either via the checkbox on "
"the Ribbon or via the settings in the `xlwings.conf` sheet)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:12
msgid ""
"Add the directory of your Python source file to the `PYTHONPATH`---again, "
"either via Ribbon or `xlwings.conf` sheet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:14
msgid ""
"If you are using the PRO version, you could instead also embed your code to "
"get around these issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:16
msgid "For a bit more flexibility, follow the solutions below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:18
msgid "OneDrive (Personal)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:20
msgid ""
"Default setups work out-of-the-box on Windows and macOS. If you get an error "
"message, add the following setting with the correct path to the local root "
"directory of your OneDrive. If possible, make use of environment variables "
"(as shown in the examples) so the configuration will work across different "
"users with the same setup:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:22
msgid "**Windows** (Example):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:24
msgid "| `ONEDRIVE_CONSUMER_WIN` | `%USERPROFILE%\\OneDrive` |"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:26
msgid "**macOS** (Example):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:28
msgid "| `ONEDRIVE_CONSUMER_MAC` | `$HOME/OneDrive` |"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:30
msgid "OneDrive for Business"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:32
msgid ""
"**Windows**: Default setups work out-of-the-box. If you get an error "
"message, add the following setting with the correct path to the local root "
"directory of your OneDrive for Business. If possible, make use of "
"environment variables (as shown in the examples) so the configuration will "
"work across different users with the same setup:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:34
msgid ""
"| `ONEDRIVE_COMMERCIAL_WIN` | `%USERPROFILE%\\OneDrive - My Company LLC` |"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:36
msgid ""
"**macOS**: macOS *always* requires the following setting with the correct "
"path to the local root directory of your OneDrive for Business. If possible, "
"make use of environment variables (as shown in the examples) so the "
"configuration will work across different users with the same setup:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:38
msgid "| `ONEDRIVE_COMMERCIAL_MAC` | `$HOME/OneDrive - My Company LLC` |"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:40
msgid "SharePoint (Online and On-Premises)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:42
msgid ""
"On Windows, the location of the local root folder of SharePoint can "
"*sometimes* be derived from the OneDrive environment variables. Most of the "
"time though, you'll have to provide the following setting (on macOS this is "
"a must):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:44
msgid "**Windows**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:46
msgid "| `SHAREPOINT_WIN` | `%USERPROFILE%\\My Company LLC` |"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:48
msgid "**macOS**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:50
msgid "| `SHAREPOINT_MAC` | `$HOME/My Company LLC` |"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:52
msgid "Implementation Details & Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:54
msgid ""
"A lot of the xlwings functionality depends on the workbook's `FullName` "
"property (via VBA/COM) that returns the local path of the file unless it is "
"saved on OneDrive, OneDrive for Business or SharePoint **with AutoSave "
"enabled**. In this case, it returns a URL instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:56
msgid ""
"URLs for OneDrive and OneDrive for Business can be translated fairly "
"straight forward to the local equivalent. You will need to know the root "
"directory of the local drive though: on Windows, these are usually provided "
"via environment variables for OneDrive. On macOS they don't exist, which is "
"the reason why you need to provide the root directory for OneDrive. On "
"Windows, the root directory for SharePoint can sometimes be derived from the "
"env vars, too, but this is not guaranteed. On macOS, you'll need to provide "
"it always anyway."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:58
msgid ""
"SharePoint, unfortunately, allows you to map the drives locally in any way "
"you want and there's no way to reliably get the local path for these files. "
"On Windows, xlwings first checks the registry for the mapping. If this "
"doesn't work, xlwings checks if the local path is mapped by using the "
"defaults and if the file can't be found, it checks all existing local files "
"on SharePoint. If it finds one with the same name, it'll use this. If, "
"however, it finds more than one with the same name, you will get an error "
"message. In this case, you can either rename the file to something unique "
"across all the locally synced SharePoint files or you can change the "
"`SHAREPOINT_WIN/MAC` setting to not stop at the root folder but include "
"additional folders. As an example, assume you have the following file "
"structure on your local SharePoint:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:68
msgid ""
"In this case, you could either rename one of the files, or you could add a "
"path that goes beyond the root folder (preferably under the `xlwings.conf` "
"sheet):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../onedrive_sharepoint.md:70
msgid ""
"| `SHAREPOINT_WIN` | `%USERPROFILE%/My Company LLC/sitename2 - Documents` |"
msgstr ""
